                <pb facs="0434" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg354"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wilson to Mr.
                            Kato.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-02-05"><hi rendition="#small-caps">February</hi> 5,
                            1901</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Ministre</hi>: Under telegraphic
                    instructions from the Secretary of State, I have the honor to request, through
                    your excellency, on behalf of the Government of the United States, that the
                    Imperial Japanese Government be so good as to further withhold their decision on
                    the questions of property leases, their registration, etc., until the Department
                    of State can have time to prepare and forward its views.</p>
                <p>Trusting that I shall soon be able to make to your excellency more detailed
                    communication of my Government’s position on all the allied questions indicated
                    above,</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
